        "category": "classfeature",
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>Something alive is wearing you. It is your weapon, your armour, and the thing that breaks.</p><p><strong>Carapace Strike.</strong> Your unarmed attack is the class. It deals <strong>1d8 bludgeoning</strong> damage, is in the <strong>brawling</strong> group, and has only the <strong>unarmed</strong> trait &mdash; it is not agile and it is not finesse. <em>Handwraps of mighty blows</em> work normally; the class grants no free fundamental runes.</p><p><strong>Living Plate.</strong> The symbiont is your armour and cannot be removed: explorer's clothing that is alive (AC item bonus +0, Dex cap +5, no check or Speed penalty, no Bulk). It accepts armour potency, resilient and property runes on the normal schedule. It has <strong>Hardness 2</strong> plus the highest Hardness bonus among your bound Substrates, <strong>10 + 5 per level</strong> Hit Points, and a Broken Threshold of half its Hit Points.</p><p><strong>Carapace Block</strong> is how the plate takes a blow for you. While the Carapace is broken, you lose Living Plate's rune benefits, and every Mutation at Depth 3 or higher switches off until it is repaired.</p>"
        },
